So, so many of the
things that I believe are

00:00:55.443 --> 00:00:59.635
going on and could impact an iconic,

00:00:59.635 --> 00:01:02.600
very large scale business like this

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:05.620
is widely available on YouTube or LinkedIn

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:07.699
and so I want to be a little
bit more specific or nuanced.

00:01:07.699 --> 00:01:10.300
I think, to set up the framework

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:13.650
because I'm gonna assume
most people don't know me

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:15.163
or where I stand on this,

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:20.120
I believe that the enormous
technology advances

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:23.060
that I'm sure especially a
company like this understands

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:26.640
and then the nuance is
underneath that infrastructure,

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:30.530
I think that the collective in
this room, including myself,

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:34.400
grossly underestimate
what it all actually means

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.950
and because it's so big, it's so heavy,

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:39.920
it's so transformative,
if you just think about,

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:41.790
and kind of looking around the room here,

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:43.230
a lot of people gonna be able to do this,

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:47.440
if you truly spent a
half a day with yourself

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.730
over, you know, a nice
walk or a bottle of wine

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:52.110
or however you like
decompress and think about

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:54.570
what has happened in technology advances

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:58.480
just in the last 20 years
it gets quite scary.

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.720
Obviously you guys do a great
job physically showing that

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.860
with mobile devices and the progression

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:05.481
but just the whole nut,
everything I believe in,

00:02:05.481 --> 00:02:10.411
and my passion is how communication

00:02:10.411 --> 00:02:13.450
basically dictates
everything we do, right.

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:17.570
I was born in this Soviet
Union and so I grew up in a,

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.640
I was born in a place of communism

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:22.350
and then I was able to
immigrate to the US,

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:25.177
a place of capitalism and media

00:02:25.177 --> 00:02:27.810
and a very different
point of view and I think

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:30.315
in a lot of ways I was very, in hindsight,

00:02:30.315 --> 00:02:33.720
taken aback by that or think about that,

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.720
I constantly think about why

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:38.700
when there is a coup in a country

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.610
do they go to the newspaper and radio

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:41.940
and television station first

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:43.930
before they even go to the palace

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:46.230
and it's because it's the punchline.

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:49.710
The thing that has the
control is communication.

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:53.580
And I think as a matter of fact,
this argument, this debate,

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:55.930
this passion I've had
for the last 15 years

00:02:55.930 --> 00:02:57.830
has become much more obvious to people

00:02:57.830 --> 00:02:59.960
as the political landscape has changed

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:02.639
across the globe very much on the back

00:03:02.639 --> 00:03:05.550
of the modern technology revolution

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:06.950
when it comes to communication.

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:11.950
And for me where I get really
excited as a businessperson

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:16.747
is when I'm met with the
best products or services

00:03:16.747 --> 00:03:19.990
that are not necessarily winning the game,

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:22.830
that they're up to completely and utterly

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:26.310
on the back of brand
perception or execution

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:28.450
of communication at this moment.

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:31.632
And so I couldn't imagine for example,

00:03:31.632 --> 00:03:34.020
and not knowing everybody's business units

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:34.853
or what you work on,

00:03:34.853 --> 00:03:37.590
but every time I go to
a remarkable company

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:40.650
inevitably there's a high
percentage of people in the room

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:41.940
that are working on something

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:46.020
where they are disproportionally
the leader in quality

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:48.200
but the business results are not matching

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:52.414
that product or service completely
and utterly predicated on

00:03:52.414 --> 00:03:55.920
either, A, you know, being way too much

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:57.300
of a sales organization

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:59.505
and not a marketing brand organization

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:04.505
or B, not even thinking about
how the actual decision maker

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.430
is being affected to make a decision

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:09.410
and where can we reach them
and how and what have you.

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:13.972
And so for me stumbling into
the talent, the natural talent,

00:04:13.972 --> 00:04:17.777
that very nice bio, what
I realized from having,

00:04:17.777 --> 00:04:19.710
and this might sound very interesting

00:04:19.710 --> 00:04:21.590
and it took me a long time to realize it,

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:24.230
the reason I had eight
lemonade stands, and I did,

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:26.700
the reason I had eight
lemonade stands as a child

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:30.258
which is absurd and very unique is

00:04:30.258 --> 00:04:33.220
on a stage like this
actually five years ago

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:35.690
I'm giving the story, I
used to give my bio more,

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:38.070
and I actually remembered
for the first time,

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:39.636
why was I doing that?

00:04:39.636 --> 00:04:40.899
Because I was starting to get

00:04:40.899 --> 00:04:42.700
a little bit upset with myself,

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:44.893
was I lazy and just one
of my friends to work?

00:04:44.893 --> 00:04:47.840
But what I was actually
doing as a six year old kid,

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:51.007
as a six year old child, I was walking,

00:04:51.007 --> 00:04:54.300
the 1980s and America was much more safe,

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:56.440
so I was walking about in the neighborhood

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:59.760
and I was looking at the cars driving

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:04.706
and trying to figure out where
to put my lemonade stand sign

00:05:04.706 --> 00:05:09.706
on which tree or which post of a sign

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:15.400
and basically 37 years
later right here right now

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:17.330
I'm still doing the same thing.

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:20.921
I've been chasing the
attention of human beings

00:05:20.921 --> 00:05:24.770
to figure out where
they're paying attention

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:27.470
and then I spend the rest of my time

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:30.700
trying to make a sign
that's gonna make them stop

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:32.520
and buy my lemonade.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:35.893
And I very successfully did
that for my father's business

00:05:35.893 --> 00:05:40.040
on the back of modern
communication technology advances.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:42.841
The reason I was able to
build a small wine shop

00:05:42.841 --> 00:05:47.200
into a national player in no
time with no venture capital,

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:49.090
nope, not even a credit line,

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:50.690
working with my own small capital,

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:53.790
three million dollar business
doing 10% gross profit.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:56.140
To build that to 60 million
with no cash infusion

00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:58.430
in five years takes one move,

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:02.170
a remarkable ability to make
every penny work like a dollar

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:03.460
in acquiring customers.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:04.670
How did I do that?

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:07.800
I did that with email
marketing and Google AdWords

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.267
because that was the enormous arbitrage

00:06:10.267 --> 00:06:14.497
in the market from 1996 to 2001.

00:06:14.497 --> 00:06:17.710
An arbitrage and an understanding
of consumer behavior

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:20.730
that my competitive
landscape did not understand.

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:23.540
That has basically become the seed

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:25.860
that allowed me to later
be an early investor

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:27.520
in Facebook and Twitter and Tumblr

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:30.798
because I viewed them as
the next paradigm shifts

00:06:30.798 --> 00:06:33.150
and it's what makes me think every night

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:35.020
about voice-activated devices

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:36.840
with AI infrastructure behind them

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:40.537
because every consumer picks
convenience over everything

00:06:40.537 --> 00:06:44.010
and will use those
devices to make decisions

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:47.771
and then that becomes the new
toll booth to transactions.

00:06:47.771 --> 00:06:50.310
That's very consumer centric,

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:51.850
very much what I think about

00:06:51.850 --> 00:06:53.850
when I think about a company like this

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:57.080
is how does that translate
to a B2B environment?

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:59.506
How does that translate to the cliche

00:06:59.506 --> 00:07:02.410
things that are at friction to my beliefs

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:07.300
with an engineer sales
DNA driven organization?

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:09.730
And it plays out in
many ways but ultimately

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:11.460
what I think it plays out in is

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:14.210
I genuinely believe for this company

00:07:14.210 --> 00:07:16.900
to take full advantage of 49,000 patents,

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:20.257
to take full advantage of
the speed in which it's

00:07:20.257 --> 00:07:22.547
deployed to become a leader in 5G

00:07:22.547 --> 00:07:25.060
and many other things that
I'm sure people are proud of

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:27.632
or the innovations that are
happening throughout the globe

00:07:27.632 --> 00:07:31.710
is A, ironically to become
a media company itself.

00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:34.210
And when I say media I mean publishing.

00:07:34.210 --> 00:07:36.240
I think over the next decade or two

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:39.000
you will see companies like
yourselves and your competitors

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:41.910
start to realize an editor-in-chief

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:45.270
will sit at the highest
levels in a company like this

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:49.933
because actually being
publishing DNA is imperative.

00:07:49.933 --> 00:07:53.066
Which is extremely difficult for a company

00:07:53.066 --> 00:07:55.310
because if you're gonna be a publisher

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:58.170
you need to be a publisher,
which is very different

00:07:58.170 --> 00:08:00.270
than being an advertiser.

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:03.590
You know, putting out content
that has no direct attribution

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:06.230
to something that you can
measure in the short term

00:08:06.230 --> 00:08:10.640
as a funnel to a sales
center to a transaction

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:11.950
takes a level of discipline,

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:13.820
especially if somebody's held accountable

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:15.797
for every 90 days or every year

00:08:15.797 --> 00:08:18.930
but that will be the requirement

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:23.170
because a word that has been
really running through my head

00:08:23.170 --> 00:08:26.130
quite a bit over the last
couple of years as entitlement.

00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:28.630
Mainly because I have
exploded on Instagram

00:08:28.630 --> 00:08:33.037
and I get 10,000 direct
messages a week from kids

00:08:33.037 --> 00:08:38.037
who are wealthy, affluent,
being totally taken care of

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:42.330
and they hate their parents
for creating entitlement

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:44.160
and they don't know how to get out of it.

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:45.470
But they're making a lot of excuses,

00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:47.150
that's a different story.

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:51.030
But what I realize is that
same thing that a 19 year old

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:53.420
whose parents have paid for everything

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:56.390
and she or he is realizing
wait a minute I'm a zoo animal

00:08:56.390 --> 00:08:58.807
and I don't know how to live in the wild,

00:08:58.807 --> 00:09:01.329
I believe there's a level of entitlement

00:09:01.329 --> 00:09:05.800
that is rampant amongst the Fortune 500

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:09.030
or biggest companies in
the world of thinking

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:11.040
that they're entitled to the business.

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:15.110
They make audacious points of view

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:16.460
on their competitive landscape,

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:19.450
they say silly things like,

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:24.250
make razzes and jokes
about emerging competitors

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:26.480
who eventually become their biggest issues

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:28.410
and I've been thinking
quite a bit about that.

00:09:28.410 --> 00:09:30.080
And I think it all leads

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:32.050
to actually a very interesting place

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:36.260
which is ultimately both
high net-worth parents

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:38.330
and executives of very big companies

00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:40.853
unfortunately are not consumer centric.

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:45.930
Unfortunately play within
their B2B confines.

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:49.340
Score on different metrics
than the actual end user

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:50.930
that they're supposed to be deploying for.

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:55.420
And so my luck, and
that's what I'll call it,

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:59.190
of DNA of only ever being consumer centric

00:09:59.190 --> 00:10:02.390
has led to the honor of
sitting here and talking to you

00:10:02.390 --> 00:10:05.460
and having people pay attention
and all the nice things

00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:07.490
that have happened to me and it's fun

00:10:07.490 --> 00:10:10.170
because there's nothing
more entrepreneurial

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:13.460
or rogue or disruptive
than actually caring

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:16.310
about nothing in the middle
but the end consumer.

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:19.920
Pandering to nothing, not
awards, not the press,

00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:22.690
not the media, not the B2B environments,

00:10:22.690 --> 00:10:25.639
not the conferences not
the people that are fancy,

00:10:25.639 --> 00:10:29.690
just the end consumer and
building leverage there

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:31.460
which ultimately gives you leverage

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:33.130
with all the things that I just mentioned

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:34.260
that are in the middle.

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:37.330
And so for me what that all,

00:10:37.330 --> 00:10:39.695
all that pontificating
leads to the following,

00:10:39.695 --> 00:10:42.231
Ericsson should be putting out

00:10:42.231 --> 00:10:46.253
250 pieces of LinkedIn creative a day.

00:10:47.383 --> 00:10:52.383
And it probably puts
out three, nine, seven,

00:10:52.390 --> 00:10:55.540
and more importantly,
is that picture, video,

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:57.930
and written article white paper?

00:10:57.930 --> 00:11:01.600
Is that been contextually post produced

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:05.130
for the understanding of how
LinkedIn algorithm works?

00:11:05.130 --> 00:11:10.130
Does it understand that the
adjectives used in the copy

00:11:10.340 --> 00:11:13.080
change the difference of
37,000 people seeing it

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:15.740
versus 2.9 million people seeing it?

00:11:15.740 --> 00:11:18.690
Is it a video that people
actually want to watch

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:21.287
or was it a video that
somebody wanted to make

00:11:21.287 --> 00:11:23.643
because it makes them feel
good of what it looks like?

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:27.150
Does it ladder up to the brand

00:11:27.150 --> 00:11:29.310
which is a complete exercise of executives

00:11:29.310 --> 00:11:31.470
making subjective calls?

00:11:31.470 --> 00:11:34.520
Unfortunately so much
of what big companies do

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:38.500
is an insular game of
politics pandering to reports

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:41.620
that mean nothing and a lot of
other things that ultimately

00:11:41.620 --> 00:11:44.517
become the demise of great
companies and it makes sense

00:11:44.517 --> 00:11:46.830
but it doesn't have to be that way.

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:49.570
And the place that I
think is most practical

00:11:49.570 --> 00:11:51.840
to actually make a hard change

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:53.960
is marketing and communication.

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:58.940
It's very hard to make a
quick change on your product,

00:11:58.940 --> 00:12:01.980
it's more difficult to
change your culture,

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:04.940
you know, there's a lot of
things that are a challenge

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:09.140
but not wasting your media money

00:12:09.140 --> 00:12:12.138
on television commercials
that nobody watches,

00:12:12.138 --> 00:12:14.920
banner ads that nobody clicks

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:17.970
and millions of other
executions that make no sense

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:20.740
other than to the bullshit
reports that sit in the middle

00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:23.100
to justify the bad behavior

00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:25.000
is something I have an
enormous passion for.

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:29.953
Especially when you have
what I call sawdust.

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:33.200
I'm super fascinated by sawdust.

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:36.430
At some point in our world somebody looked

00:12:36.430 --> 00:12:38.210
at people cutting wood and said,

00:12:38.210 --> 00:12:39.500
the stuff that's going on the ground

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:41.490
is something I can sell.

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:42.860
and I think about that a lot,

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:45.730
I also, bottled water is the
much more interesting one.

00:12:45.730 --> 00:12:48.980
I would probably pay an
uncomfortable amount of money

00:12:48.980 --> 00:12:53.550
to have the right to in a
VR setting sit in the room

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:55.810
with whoever she or he was that decided

00:12:55.810 --> 00:12:57.520
this was gonna actually play out

00:12:57.520 --> 00:12:59.980
selling something that
was free to the world

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:01.820
because as a marketer as you can imagine,

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:04.550
that is a very fascinating execution.

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:08.350
But that's actually how I
view a company like this.

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:11.105
If you think about the sheer amount

00:13:11.105 --> 00:13:14.973
of sawdust in the form of unbelievably

00:13:14.973 --> 00:13:19.220
compelling tech stories

00:13:19.220 --> 00:13:21.670
that happened in the halls globally

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:23.890
around the 100,000 people
that are touching this place

00:13:23.890 --> 00:13:28.890
